# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AP-Harness-QC governance and artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Two logs, deliberately split by audience and destination.
#
# TRACKED: CLAUDE_LOG.md at the repository root, the project progress and
# decision record. It is project output: what was decided, when, and why.
#
# IGNORED: the prompt log. Verbatim prompts, phrasings and working notes are
# material for later review rather than project output, and they are the one
# place a credential could be pasted by accident.
.claude/logs/

# Private design notes. The tracked designs state the integration contract
# generically, as standard artifact formats any collector can read. Naming a
# specific downstream consumer would couple a public repository to a choice
# that may change, so concrete detail lives here instead.
.claude/notes/

# Everything else under .claude/ IS tracked. The rule files are the governance
# layer this project partly exists to demonstrate, so they belong in the repo.

# Design and test-design documents are tracked project output, not scratch
# work. Listed explicitly so a later blanket docs/ rule cannot silently drop
# them.
!docs/
!docs/design/
!docs/design/**
!docs/testing/
!docs/testing/**

# CI-generated test artifacts. Regenerated every run and published to GitHub
# Actions, which is where downstream collection reads them from; committing
# them would duplicate the artifact store in git to no benefit.
reports/
allure-results/
allure-report/
junit_*.xml

# Provider credentials. Never committed, never written into design documents
# or logs. The example file IS tracked and contains no real key.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# JetBrains IDE settings. Machine-local and developer-specific: committing
# them makes every teammate editor state a source of merge conflicts. The
# GitHub template ships this line commented out, which reads as present to a
# careless grep and ignores nothing.
.idea/
